{# Widget "ledger" — every fact as a column (FL·05).

   STATIC TWIN of files.widgets.js's `ledger` entry. Rendered by BOTH the hub and
   the widget library.

   The same result set as `browse`, in its list shape, without the chrome. The
   only shape that answers the storage questions in one look. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiStorage/files/_ui.html.twig' as ui %}
<div class="c" data-w="ledger">
    <span class="tab">The file ledger<span class="src">&middot; every fact, none of the pictures</span></span>
    <table class="f-list" data-f-list>{{ ui.listhead() }}<tbody>{%- for file in files -%}{{ ui.row(file, places) }}{%- endfor -%}</tbody></table>
    {% if files is empty %}{{ ui.empty(true) }}{% endif %}
    <div class="use">The only shape that answers the storage questions in one look: <b>which files have no small picture</b>, <b>what is kept where</b>, and <b>what a record is actually costing</b>. Click any row for the picture.</div>
</div>